{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-4","kind":"proposition","title":"求三个可公度量的最大公度","englishTitle":"Given three commensurable magnitudes, to find their greatest common measure.","book":10,"number":4,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.4","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.4/","group":"prop_1","sourceNumber":4,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","contentId":"euclid-10-4","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"883fe608ee23f99b47c4a378dbdf6f3b6a7eba2ff40b1a4899bc6dc5620e53da","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-4.statement","euclid-10-4.construction.1","euclid-10-4.construction.2","euclid-10-4.proof.1","euclid-10-4.proof.2","euclid-10-4.proof.3","euclid-10-4.proof.4","euclid-10-4.proof.5","euclid-10-4.proof.6","euclid-10-4.proof.7","euclid-10-4.proof.8","euclid-10-4.proof.9","euclid-10-4.proof.10","euclid-10-4.proof.11","euclid-10-4.proof.12","euclid-10-4.proof.13","euclid-10-4.proof.14","euclid-10-4.proof.15","euclid-10-4.proof.16","euclid-10-4.proof.17","euclid-10-4.proof.18","euclid-10-4.proof.19","euclid-10-4.conclusion","euclid-10-4.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-4.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"884ba7b34268c12d3e0a10fa2fe4e58c521111263981d8be553e4d7a7c645818","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Given three commensurable magnitudes, to find their greatest common measure."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"以三度可公度的高度 来找到最共同的量度；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f3d5a559e03eb23ab02f9a01d9a7b167fc2208f3db08cfeecd68a29626c51cd6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let A, B, C be the three given commensurable magnitudes; thus it is required to find the greatest common measure of A, B, C."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让A,B,C是给定的可公度等;因此,需要找到最大共同度量,即A,B,C；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":2,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"98f1f032b1ebd44f26fac10229d9ca1965d4dffe63498abd1a36370679a64126","citations":["euclid-10-3"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let the greatest common measure of the two magnitudes A, B be taken, and let it be D; [[X. 3](/principles/euclid-10-3)] then D either measures C, or does not measure it."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"采取A,B这两个尺度中最大的共同尺度,然后是D;然后是D,要么C,要么不计量；其中所求的量是最大公约数。 [[X. 3](/principles/euclid-10-3)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"417172124a383d5eb40b139503383efeb7cf5d197da3c58bd3e953cd3ad77efa","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"First, let it measure it."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"首先,让它整除它。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"05f2f22d570b0471cccb050eeef46a6de4edef522ff7a76c68488993dc2336a8","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since then D measures C, while it also measures A, B, therefore D is a common measure of A, B, C."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"自那以后,共有D项措施C,同时,A、B项措施,因此,共有D项措施A、B、C项。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"03f481fb13334775ae4b314c1576490723651a8a6a1f216d43f31954cb262e2c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And it is manifest that it is also the greatest; for a greater magnitude than the magnitude D does not measure A, B."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"很明显,它也是最大的;比D的大小大,不能测量A,B。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"fd907842b073f2273e8018b3d70b6fb8dea6af594273a75337248526ff22e16f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Next, let D not measure C."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"接下来,让D不测量C。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8ea719989b58a180ff68e9d54bce0bba42a2686328d7ec0585f57af896e851a4","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"I say first that C, D are commensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"我首先说C,D是可公度"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"358c215e5c4063f6edca4d75f2e0269a1c70958b6d195ab0ffdb828c90dd1f3c","citations":["euclid-10-3"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since A, B, C are commensurable, some magnitude will measure them, and this will of course measure A, B also; so that it will also measure the greatest common measure of A, B, namely D. [[X. 3, Por.](/principles/euclid-10-3)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为,A,B,C是可公度, 一定的量度它们, 当然,这也会测量A,B; 这样它就能测量A,B这个最大共同度量,即D；其中所求的量是最大公约数。 [[X. 3, Por.](/principles/euclid-10-3)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"842a970df3410854d24a015cbb1f8421af932fd962f3cb9dc4241958472cfe2c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it also measures C; so that the said magnitude will measure C, D; therefore C, D are commensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,它也衡量C;因此,上述数量将衡量C,D;因此,C,D是可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":10,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d70d566785ad0e603e7425bfd19da823a3b4e93ae8550ba5b7b35f91ac4e0b2d","citations":["euclid-10-3"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now let their greatest common measure be taken, and let it be E. [[X. 3](/principles/euclid-10-3)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在让它们采取最共同的措施,让E采取；其中所求的量是最大公约数。 [[X. 3](/principles/euclid-10-3)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.9","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":11,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 9","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"88cc3a94406468f36308615fa05a3e883450fba348f4180b431d7900d372ba1c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since then E measures D, while D measures A, B, therefore E will also measure A, B."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"此后,E项措施D项,D项措施A、B项,因此E项措施A、B项。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.10","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":12,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 10","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c35cb459525c1acafffa86f9d705fecdcf372d8100d38c932f31e2e8b7061102","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures C also; therefore E measures A, B, C; therefore E is a common measure of A, B, C."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但它也为整除 C;因此,E 整除 A,B,C;因此,E是A,B,C的共同整除。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.11","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":13,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 11","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8d601a2226cb30a3cfb5f77868366f58ff9f45ffd66f31803b59b1f868041374","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"I say next that it is also the greatest."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"我接下来说,这也是最伟大的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.12","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":14,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 12","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"839ac521815419c3279f570b99869b887cbd150cb7a9b73ba72e91026cc80db7","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if possible, let there be some magnitude F greater than E, and let it measure A, B, C."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果可能的话,让我们用F的尺寸超过E, 并用它来测量A,B,C。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.13","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":15,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 13","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"93d8e9eb9b0863b0a33935756941eacf87f8ce857e4ca504b707506dbba11c6e","citations":["euclid-10-3"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now, since F measures A, B, C, it will also measure A, B, and will measure the greatest common measure of A, B. [[X. 3, Por.](/principles/euclid-10-3)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,自F项措施A、B、C项措施以来,还将对A、B项措施进行衡量,并将对A、B项最常用措施进行衡量；其中所求的量是最大公约数。 [[X. 3, Por.](/principles/euclid-10-3)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.14","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":16,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 14","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"07cb3d899ba685ee3a3937b89cfac567c959b8e9b0bd06969429096278940254","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the greatest common measure of A, B is D; therefore F measures D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但A中最大公约数,B为D,因此F 整除 D。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.15","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":17,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 15","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c7a9bd76bb217c56f7c1eee8c0d0918ef27a8577105d061a5b93176cf0b598a1","citations":["euclid-10-3"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures C also; therefore F measures C, D; therefore F will also measure the greatest common measure of C, D. [[X. 3, Por.](/principles/euclid-10-3)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但该标准也为C项;因此,F项措施为C项,D项;因此,F项措施也将测量C项,D项这一最大共同标准；其中所求的量是最大公约数。 [[X. 3, Por.](/principles/euclid-10-3)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.16","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":18,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 16","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7488e2c1cd1fe794249ecadcd47f588081e9dd99c5d41bb34b261958bd0bc5e2","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But that is E; therefore F will measure E, the greater the less: which is impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但这是E, 因此F将测量E, 数量越大,数量越小:这是不可能的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.17","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":19,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 17","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"014adad2dd3c4b5b1a8d02fc657c6110740094454a2ad53431d9771944e96b36","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore no magnitude greater than the magnitude E will measure A, B, C; therefore E is the greatest common measure of A, B, C if D do not measure C, and, if it measure it, D is itself the greatest common measure."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,如果D不测量C,则E星等的大小不能测量A,B,C;因此,E是最大的通用量值,即A,B,C,D,如果测量不到C,则D是最大的通用量值；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.18","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":20,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 18","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"dd62c39134cd0f0cb7ae5884e535fff1955adc9c2c6341b316595489909f861e","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the greatest common measure of the three given commensurable magnitudes has been found."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,发现了三种给定可公度级的最大共同度量；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.proof.19","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":21,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 19","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"5d76c0c06234b1af0f783c1935572382d154ce1380f92b47d590fad897513cf9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Porism. From this it is manifest that, if a magnitude measure three magnitudes, it will also measure their greatest common measure."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"推论,从这一点来看,很明显,如果一个量测量三个量,它也会测量它们最大的共同度量；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":22,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7f879bb4fae0b54ba3104d4511d579bc2ed0881341f520ac614d9430b067097e","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Similarly too, with more magnitudes, the greatest common measure can be found, and the porism can be extended. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,如果数量更多,可以找到最大的共同尺度,而龙石柱也可以延长；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-4.source","contentId":"euclid-10-4","revisionId":"euclid-10-4@raw-883fe608ee23f99b","order":23,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f20f686823ef3f3a478b0da4e3e246fc533d5d4514d6a5389d0d1eb588408305","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.4/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.4\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-4:euclid-10-3:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-4","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-4.construction.2","euclid-10-4.proof.6","euclid-10-4.proof.8","euclid-10-4.proof.13","euclid-10-4.proof.15"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-3","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.4","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.4/","sourceLabel":"X. 3"}}],"incomingEdges":[],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-10-4:euclid-10-3:explicit","id":"euclid-10-3","book":10,"number":3,"kind":"proposition","title":"求两个可公度量的最大公度","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"dependents":[],"visualization":{"level":"concept_illustration","rendererId":"concept-irrational","rationale":"The current renderer is selected by a broad geometry family and must not be presented as this proposition’s exact construction."},"sourceIssues":[]}
